00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Michael Che.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:52.385 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hi.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.655 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Isn't this something?

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Isn't this great?

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is good.
This is good. Oh!

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome, buddy.
-How are you?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.064
-I mean, you've done a coupl
of these with no audiences

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I have.
-How is it --

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.100 line:92%
I know it's not full at "SNL,"

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it really does feel full
at home watching.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.605 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It feels amazing now.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it feels really,
really great.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I don't know
how many people's in there

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.979
but you start to forget what
it was like when it was packed

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:24.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. You just needed to set
a new baseline, and now --

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and it's also
kind of cool

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.855
because you can hear, like
you know, specific things,

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.256 line:92%
like, "That wasn't funny."

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, it's nice.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.460 line:92%
Sometimes when it gets too full,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can't hear, like,
specific in-the-moment notes

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember me and Jost
did Mania,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:41.134 line:92%
and it was in MetLife Stadium.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was like 80,000,
90,000 people,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:44.771 line:92%
this big wrestling event.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:48.775
And we went out, and you
just hear the roar of boos

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.442 size:75% position:38% line:92%
which we're used to.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.145
But then if you made eye contact
with somebody,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.380
you can hear specifically
what they were saying about you,

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.118
what they hated about you,
and that was a lot more intense.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The best one
that ever happened to me

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.389 line:92%
was when I was doing "Update."

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.591 line:92%
My parents were in the audience.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I told one joke
that bombed with everyone,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
except my mom
laughed really loud.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:13.299
And I got -- My brother wrote me
an e-mail the next day

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.868 line:92%
that said, "Well, Mom liked it."

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That's great.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did one I think
like two weeks ago.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.942
I don't even -- if it was my
joke or if it was Colin's joke

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.211 line:92%
But one lady just said, "No.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, no? What do you mean, no
That's not an option.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've talked
to some people who --

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was more before
it got too cold to do it,

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:36.022
people that were doing outdoor
shows, maybe like September.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.223 line:92%
And they were saying, one,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
they had to remember
how to be a stand-up again

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they also
felt like the audience

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
had to remember
how to be audiences again.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:48.434
-Yeah, I mean, stand-up's a lo
harder than being an audience.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's probably
harder for them

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're not being
very funny onstage, you know

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.876 size:88% position:44%
'Cause stand-up is a lot
about just remembering

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.077 line:92%
and timing and all of that

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.078 line:92%
And when you don't have that

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
it does look like
a guy just talking,

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is something
nobody really wants.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:07.353
-Right, everybody wants to d
but nobody wants to watch.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
Exactly.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.790
-Yeah, people are like, "Oh,
my God, I'd love a microphon

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be allowed to talk
for an hour."

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
It has been --
You have three shows left.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-A weird season.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-An incredible accomplishmen
that you guys got --

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're gonna get through it,
knock on wood.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, we've had some really
really cool guests.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had Chappelle.
We had Burr.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had Daniel Kaluuya.
We had Issa Rae.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We had Regina King.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:31.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we had an amazing season
of guests, I think.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now Elon Musk
is gonna be on.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know,
that's gonna be exciting, too.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's the richest man
in the world.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
How could you not be excited
for that?

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.019 line:92%
-Do you have any interest --

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I will say,
talking about stand-ups,

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:45.091 size:81% position:41% line:92%
'cause I think that...

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obama very much had
a stand-up cadence, I thought.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I think that Trum
sort of had stand-up material.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.366 line:92%
He was, like, working on an act.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:56.302 size:84% position:42%
-That's the best way
I've ever heard it put.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obama has the cadence,
and Trump has the material

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.174 line:92%
-He's just been working at -

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:01.908 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And one of the funniest

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.344
where I was genuinely like, "Oh,
that's a good stand-up bit,"

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:08.081
is he used to talk about how all
rich people want to go to space.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh,
that's a pretty good premise

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.184 size:75% position:38% line:92%
for a stand-up bit."

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really good.
It's very rich.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.821 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Can we laugh at him now?

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.521 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Who, Trump?

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.090 line:92%
-Yeah, can we laugh with him

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.692 line:92%
-Oh, can we laugh with him

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.360 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Different question.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When are we allowed
to laugh with him again?

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.630 size:75% position:38%
-When are we allowed
to laugh with Trump

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.999
and say, "You know what?
That one was really funny.

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:29.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you have any interest
in going to space?

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I mean, not first.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:33.840 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Not first.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.542
I didn't want to be first
to get the vaccine, man.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.711 line:92%
We're very paranoid people

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Well, I mean, I think -- Yeah.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:44.917
If Elon said, though, if he wa
going and he invited you to go

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He'd have to FaceTime me
from there.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:47.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:50.957
-And I'd have to be certai
that he was actually there

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you're
a history buff,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.394 line:92%
but we've been tricked before.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
A very funny clip
with you and Cecily.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've only watched
the first episode,

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I was telling you
backstage I think is great

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.538 line:92%
It will come to no surpris

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
to anyone who knows
the way you write

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.743
and the way you do stand-up,
this show is not entirely,

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
but a good deal about race
-Yes.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.547 line:92%
-And the thing I cannot fathom

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.015 size:81% position:41%
and I've talked to you
about this, as well,

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:18.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that you basically wrot
and did this show

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
while you were doing "SNL,
which just seems overwhelming.

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a very bad idea,
as they say in the business.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.727 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It was exhausting, man.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.596
This was, like, a really,
really exhausting year

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of doing this show.

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:35.735
We not only wrote it, but we
also shot it during "SNL."

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:38.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, like, on off weeks,
we would just be doing that.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:39.939 line:92%
So this is kind of like --

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
This next break that we have
for the season

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
will be, like, kind of my firs
actual break from anything

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I'll just be
doing stand-up.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you glad that they're all
coming out at once?

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.386
Because it must be strange
to write sketches at "SNL,

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:54.153 line:92%
which you never have to wait

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than basically five day
until you see it.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, at first,
initially I wasn't.

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
Initially I wanted to roll out
like "SNL"

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
because then you could
always improve it.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.363 line:92%
But now I'm like, "Oh, yeah,

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
it'd be either one week
of great press

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
or one week of terrible press,
and then it's over,"

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I kind of like that they'r
all kind of coming out.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can watch it
at your own leisure.

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to -- have
a lot more questions for you

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
but particularly
about the title.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back with mor
from Michael Che.

